From 5e81aef50cd4b999718eb29d5b5766fe4547594e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:38:13 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [MOS] Keep strong copy hints inside the allocation order

getRegAllocationHints returns the strong copy hint as a hard hint, but
getStrongCopyHint only checks that the hinted register belongs to the
virtual register's class. A class member can still be outside the
allocation order, for example a reserved register.

SPC700 indirect calls reach this case. Call lowering copies the JMP opcode
($5F) into the reserved RC17 and calls __rc17. On SPC700, LDImm may define
an imaginary register, so the constant's class is Anyi8, which contains
RC17. When the constant is not folded into the copy (MachineLICM or
MachineCSE often share or hoist it), its only use is the copy into RC17, so
the strong hint names RC17. With assertions, AllocationOrder::create then
fails with "Target hint is outside allocation order". Without assertions,
greedy follows the hard hint and assigns the virtual register to the
reserved RC17.

Use the strong hint only when it is in the allocation order. Otherwise fall
back to the cost-based hints, which put the value in an allocatable register
that is cheap to copy into the destination. Returning no hints with a hard
order instead would leave the rematerialized value without any register.

Every MOS CPU runs this code, but only SPC700 produces such a copy, so
generated code changes only for SPC700 functions that make indirect calls.
Those functions previously asserted with assertions enabled. Without
assertions they used a reserved register. Functions that compiled with
assertions enabled are unaffected, since the changed path always asserted.

Test: llvm/test/CodeGen/MOS/regalloc-spc700.mir.

Root cause, repair and validation: Claude Code 2.1.296, model Claude
Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5), high reasoning effort.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 llvm/lib/Target/MOS/MOSRegisterInfo.cpp   |  8 +++--
 llvm/test/CodeGen/MOS/regalloc-spc700.mir | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 llvm/test/CodeGen/MOS/regalloc-spc700.mir

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/MOS/MOSRegisterInfo.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/MOS/MOSRegisterInfo.cpp
index e6fccc3a3..d47fbd6b8 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/MOS/MOSRegisterInfo.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/MOS/MOSRegisterInfo.cpp
@@ -696,8 +696,12 @@ bool MOSRegisterInfo::getRegAllocationHints(
   for (const auto &R : enumerate(Order))
     OriginalIndex[R.value()] = R.index();
 
-  if (std::optional<Register> StrongHint =
-          getStrongCopyHint(VirtReg, MF, VRM)) {
+  // A strong hint is a hard hint, so it must come from the allocation order.
+  // A copy can still name a register outside the order, such as the reserved
+  // RC17 that SPC700 indirect calls load with a JMP opcode. The value then
+  // needs some allocatable register, so it falls back to the cost-based hints.
+  std::optional<Register> StrongHint = getStrongCopyHint(VirtReg, MF, VRM);
+  if (StrongHint && (!*StrongHint || is_contained(Order, *StrongHint))) {
     if (*StrongHint)
       Hints.insert(*StrongHint);
     return true;
diff --git a/llvm/test/CodeGen/MOS/regalloc-spc700.mir b/llvm/test/CodeGen/MOS/regalloc-spc700.mir
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..b29375e72
--- /dev/null
+++ b/llvm/test/CodeGen/MOS/regalloc-spc700.mir
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# NOTE: Assertions have been autogenerated by utils/update_mir_test_checks.py
+# RUN: llc -mtriple=mos -mcpu=mosspc700 -run-pass=greedy,virtregrewriter -verify-machineinstrs -o - %s | FileCheck %s
+
+# An SPC700 indirect call writes the JMP opcode into the reserved RC17 and
+# calls __rc17. The opcode is a rematerializable byte whose only use is the
+# copy into RC17, so the copy names a register outside the Anyi8 allocation
+# order. The allocator must place the byte in an allocatable register instead.
+---
+name: indirect_thunk_opcode
+legalized: true
+regBankSelected: true
+tracksRegLiveness: true
+body: |
+  bb.0.entry:
+    ; CHECK-LABEL: name: indirect_thunk_opcode
+    ; CHECK: renamable $x = LDImm 95
+    ; CHECK-NEXT: $rc17 = COPY killed renamable $x
+    ; CHECK-NEXT: JSR &__rc17, mos_csr, implicit $rc17
+    ; CHECK-NEXT: RTS
+    %0:anyi8 = LDImm 95
+    $rc17 = COPY %0
+    JSR &__rc17, mos_csr, implicit $rc17
+    RTS
+...
+---
+name: indirect_thunk_opcode_across_call
+legalized: true
+regBankSelected: true
+tracksRegLiveness: true
+body: |
+  bb.0.entry:
+    ; CHECK-LABEL: name: indirect_thunk_opcode_across_call
+    ; CHECK: renamable $rc20 = LDImm 95
+    ; CHECK-NEXT: JSR &fn, mos_csr
+    ; CHECK-NEXT: $rc17 = COPY killed renamable $rc20
+    ; CHECK-NEXT: JSR &__rc17, mos_csr, implicit $rc17
+    ; CHECK-NEXT: RTS
+    %0:anyi8 = LDImm 95
+    JSR &fn, mos_csr
+    $rc17 = COPY %0
+    JSR &__rc17, mos_csr, implicit $rc17
+    RTS
+...
